atic-sponsored and dated May, showed Grothman up 61-39"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a comfortable Republican win: an R+8 district, a well-funded incumbent, and a challenger with modest resources and no outside spending. Expert raters unanimously place the race at Safe or Solid R, and the lone poll showed a wide Grothman lead, so the forecast sits well to the Republican side while retaining some uncertainty from thin polling.", "watch": "A late Democratic wave or surge in anti-incumbent turnout could narrow the margin, but Smith would need a dramatic shift to contend.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Glenn Grothman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Glenn Grothman seeks another term in Wisconsin's 6th District, a seat with an R+8 partisan lean, against Democrat Brad Smith. Grothman has out-raised Smith roughly four to one and holds a large cash advantage, while Smith has drawn no outside support. The only available poll, from a Democratic-leaning sponsor in May, showed Grothman leading 61-39. Every major expert rating places the race at Safe or Solid Republican. Minor and independent candidates trail far behind in fundraising. The race has drawn local coverage of issues like the Iran war, gas prices, and immigration, but no evidence of a competitive dynamic. Grothman is a strong favorite, with the main question being the size of his winning margin rather than the outcome itself.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -10.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0701, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.063, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0353, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0532, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0212, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0386, "mar